"""Universe, Earth and life-origin answers (en/fr/rw/sw). Dates are widely accepted scientific estimates. fr/rw/sw are drafts pending fluent review."""
from knowledge_base import _e

ENTRIES_COSMOS = [
_e("big_bang", ["universe_expansion", "stars_life_cycle", "solar_system_formation"],
   ("What is the Big Bang and how did the universe begin?", "Qu'est-ce que le Big Bang et comment l'univers a-t-il commencé ?", "Big Bang ni iki kandi isanzure ryatangiye rite?", "Big Bang ni nini na ulimwengu ulianzaje?"),
   ("big bang|the big bang|how did the universe begin|origin of the universe|beginning of the universe|age of the universe|how old is the universe|universe formation|cosmic microwave background|history of the universe",
    "big bang|le big bang|comment l'univers a commence|origine de l'univers|debut de l'univers|age de l'univers|quel age a l'univers|formation de l'univers|fond diffus cosmologique|histoire de l'univers",
    "big bang|uko isanzure ryatangiye|inkomoko y'isanzure|itangira ry'isanzure|imyaka y'isanzure|isanzure rimaze imyaka ingahe|ishingwa ry'isanzure|amateka y'isanzure",
    "big bang|ulimwengu ulianzaje|asili ya ulimwengu|mwanzo wa ulimwengu|umri wa ulimwengu|ulimwengu una umri gani|kuundwa kwa ulimwengu|historia ya ulimwengu"),
   ("The Big Bang theory says the universe began about 13.8 billion years ago from an extremely hot, dense state and has been expanding and cooling ever since. It was not an explosion in space; space itself expanded. Evidence includes the expansion of galaxies, the cosmic microwave background (leftover light), and the amounts of hydrogen and helium.",
    "La théorie du Big Bang dit que l'univers a commencé il y a environ 13,8 milliards d'années à partir d'un état extrêmement chaud et dense, et qu'il se dilate et se refroidit depuis. Ce n'était pas une explosion dans l'espace ; c'est l'espace lui-même qui s'est dilaté. Les preuves : l'expansion des galaxies, le fond diffus cosmologique (lumière fossile) et les proportions d'hydrogène et d'hélium.",
    "Theory ya Big Bang ivuga ko isanzure ryatangiye hashize imyaka miliyari 13.8 riva ku mimerere ishyushye cyane kandi ifunganye, kuva icyo gihe riragenda ryaguka rigakonja. Ntabwo ari iturika mu cyogajuru; ahubwo umwanya ubwawo warazamutse. Ibimenyetso: kwaguka kw'ibyogajuru by'inyenyeri (galaxies), urumuri rusigaye (CMB), n'ingano ya hydrogen na helium.",
    "Nadharia ya Big Bang inasema ulimwengu ulianza takriban miaka bilioni 13.8 iliyopita kutoka hali yenye joto kali na msongamano mkubwa, na tangu hapo unapanuka na kupoa. Haikuwa mlipuko angani; nafasi yenyewe ilipanuka. Ushahidi: kupanuka kwa galaksi, mwanga uliobaki (CMB), na kiasi cha hidrojeni na heliamu."),
   (["About 13.8 billion years ago: the Big Bang; within minutes the first hydrogen and helium nuclei formed.", "About 380,000 years later: atoms formed and light could travel freely; we still detect it as the cosmic microwave background.", "A few hundred million years later: the first stars and galaxies formed.", "Science cannot yet say what, if anything, came before the Big Bang; that is an open question."],
    ["Il y a environ 13,8 milliards d'années : le Big Bang ; en quelques minutes, les premiers noyaux d'hydrogène et d'hélium se forment.", "Environ 380 000 ans plus tard : les atomes se forment et la lumière circule librement ; on la détecte encore comme fond diffus cosmologique.", "Quelques centaines de millions d'années plus tard : les premières étoiles et galaxies.", "La science ne peut pas encore dire ce qu'il y avait avant le Big Bang, s'il y avait quelque chose ; la question reste ouverte."],
    ["Hashize imyaka miliyari 13.8: Big Bang; mu minota mike hakozwe nuclei za mbere za hydrogen na helium.", "Nyuma y'imyaka nka 380,000: atomes zarakozwe urumuri rutangira kugenda; turacyarubona nka CMB.", "Nyuma y'imyaka miliyoni magana make: inyenyeri za mbere na galaxies byaravutse.", "Siyansi ntiramenya ibyabanje mbere ya Big Bang, niba hari ibyabayeho; ni ikibazo kikiri gifunguye."],
    ["Takriban miaka bilioni 13.8 iliyopita: Big Bang; ndani ya dakika chache viini vya kwanza vya hidrojeni na heliamu viliundwa.", "Takriban miaka 380,000 baadaye: atomu ziliundwa na mwanga ukaanza kusafiri; bado tunauona kama CMB.", "Mamia ya mamilioni ya miaka baadaye: nyota na galaksi za kwanza ziliundwa.", "Sayansi bado haiwezi kusema kilikuwepo nini kabla ya Big Bang, kama kilikuwepo; swali hilo bado liko wazi."])),

_e("universe_expansion", ["big_bang", "stars_life_cycle", "black_holes"],
   ("What is a galaxy and is the universe expanding? (dark matter, dark energy)", "Qu'est-ce qu'une galaxie et l'univers est-il en expansion ? (matière noire, énergie noire)", "Galaxy ni iki kandi isanzure riraguka? (dark matter, dark energy)", "Galaksi ni nini na ulimwengu unapanuka? (dark matter, dark energy)"),
   ("what is a galaxy|milky way|is the universe expanding|expanding universe|hubble|dark matter|dark energy|how many galaxies|observable universe|size of the universe",
    "qu'est-ce qu'une galaxie|voie lactee|l'univers est-il en expansion|univers en expansion|hubble|matiere noire|energie noire|combien de galaxies|univers observable|taille de l'univers",
    "galaxy ni iki|inzira y'amata|isanzure riraguka|isanzure rigenda ryaguka|hubble|dark matter|dark energy|galaxies zingahe|ingano y'isanzure",
    "galaksi ni nini|njia ya maziwa|ulimwengu unapanuka|ulimwengu unaopanuka|hubble|dark matter|dark energy|galaksi ngapi|ukubwa wa ulimwengu"),
   ("A galaxy is a huge system of stars, gas, dust and dark matter held together by gravity. Our galaxy is the Milky Way. In 1929 Edwin Hubble showed that distant galaxies move away from us, and the farther they are the faster they recede, which means space is expanding. The expansion is speeding up, which scientists attribute to dark energy.",
    "Une galaxie est un immense ensemble d'étoiles, de gaz, de poussière et de matière noire maintenu par la gravité. La nôtre est la Voie lactée. En 1929, Edwin Hubble a montré que les galaxies lointaines s'éloignent de nous, d'autant plus vite qu'elles sont loin : l'espace est en expansion. Cette expansion s'accélère, ce que les scientifiques attribuent à l'énergie noire.",
    "Galaxy ni ikusanyiro rinini ry'inyenyeri, imyuka, ivumbi na dark matter bifatanyirijwe hamwe na gravity. Iyacu ni Milky Way. Mu 1929 Edwin Hubble yagaragaje ko galaxies za kure zitwigirayo, kandi uko ziri kure ni ko zihuta, bivuze ko umwanya waguka. Uko kwaguka kurihuta, abahanga babyitirira dark energy.",
    "Galaksi ni mfumo mkubwa wa nyota, gesi, vumbi na dark matter unaoshikiliwa na mvutano. Yetu ni Milky Way. Mwaka 1929 Edwin Hubble alionyesha kuwa galaksi za mbali zinatuacha, na kadri zilivyo mbali ndivyo zinavyokwenda kwa kasi, maana nafasi inapanuka. Upanuzi huo unaongezeka kasi, wanasayansi wanauhusisha na dark energy."),
   (["The Milky Way holds roughly 100–400 billion stars; the observable universe holds hundreds of billions of galaxies or more.", "Observable universe: about 93 billion light-years across (a light-year is the distance light travels in one year, about 9.46 trillion km).", "Dark matter (about 27%) and dark energy (about 68%) make up most of the universe; ordinary matter is only about 5%.", "Nearest large galaxy: Andromeda, about 2.5 million light-years away."],
    ["La Voie lactée contient environ 100 à 400 milliards d'étoiles ; l'univers observable contient des centaines de milliards de galaxies ou plus.", "Univers observable : environ 93 milliards d'années-lumière de diamètre (une année-lumière est la distance parcourue par la lumière en un an, soit environ 9 460 milliards de km).", "Matière noire (environ 27 %) et énergie noire (environ 68 %) forment l'essentiel ; la matière ordinaire n'en représente que 5 % environ.", "Plus grande galaxie voisine : Andromède, à environ 2,5 millions d'années-lumière."],
    ["Milky Way ifite inyenyeri nka miliyari 100–400; isanzure rigaragara rifite galaxies amagana ya miliyari cyangwa zirenga.", "Isanzure rigaragara: ubugari bw'imyaka-urumuri nka miliyari 93 (umwaka-urumuri ni intera urumuri rugenda mu mwaka umwe, nka tiriyoni 9.46 za km).", "Dark matter (nka 27%) na dark energy (nka 68%) ni byo bigize byinshi; ibintu bisanzwe ni nka 5% gusa.", "Galaxy nini iri hafi: Andromeda, nka miliyoni 2.5 z'imyaka-urumuri."],
    ["Milky Way ina nyota takriban bilioni 100–400; ulimwengu unaoonekana una mamia ya mabilioni ya galaksi au zaidi.", "Ulimwengu unaoonekana: upana wa takriban miaka-nuru bilioni 93 (mwaka-nuru ni umbali nuru husafiri kwa mwaka mmoja, takriban trilioni 9.46 za km).", "Dark matter (takriban 27%) na dark energy (takriban 68%) hujenga sehemu kubwa; mada ya kawaida ni takriban 5% tu.", "Galaksi kubwa iliyo karibu: Andromeda, takriban miaka-nuru milioni 2.5."])),

_e("stars_life_cycle", ["black_holes", "big_bang", "solar_system_formation"],
   ("How are stars born and how do they die?", "Comment naissent et meurent les étoiles ?", "Inyenyeri zivuka zite kandi zipfa zite?", "Nyota huzaliwa na hufa vipi?"),
   ("how are stars formed|life cycle of a star|how do stars die|supernova|red giant|white dwarf|neutron star|nebula|star formation|what is a star",
    "comment se forment les etoiles|cycle de vie d'une etoile|comment meurent les etoiles|supernova|geante rouge|naine blanche|etoile a neutrons|nebuleuse|formation des etoiles|qu'est-ce qu'une etoile",
    "inyenyeri zivuka zite|ubuzima bw'inyenyeri|inyenyeri zipfa zite|supernova|red giant|white dwarf|neutron star|nebula|iyubakwa ry'inyenyeri|inyenyeri ni iki",
    "nyota huzaliwaje|mzunguko wa maisha ya nyota|nyota hufaje|supernova|red giant|white dwarf|neutron star|nebula|kuundwa kwa nyota|nyota ni nini"),
   ("A star is a huge ball of gas that shines by fusing hydrogen into helium in its core. Stars form when a cloud of gas and dust (a nebula) collapses under gravity. How a star ends depends on its mass: small stars fade slowly, while very massive stars explode as supernovae.",
    "Une étoile est une immense boule de gaz qui brille en fusionnant de l'hydrogène en hélium dans son cœur. Les étoiles naissent quand un nuage de gaz et de poussière (nébuleuse) s'effondre sous la gravité. Leur fin dépend de leur masse : les petites s'éteignent lentement, les très massives explosent en supernovae.",
    "Inyenyeri ni umupira munini w'imyuka urabagirana kubera guhuza hydrogen ikavamo helium mu mutima wayo. Inyenyeri ziravuka iyo igicu cy'imyuka n'ivumbi (nebula) gisenyutse kubera gravity. Iherezo ryayo rishingira ku bwinshi bwayo: ntoya zizima buhoro, naho nini cyane ziturika nka supernovae.",
    "Nyota ni mpira mkubwa wa gesi unaong'aa kwa kuunganisha hidrojeni kuwa heliamu katikati yake. Nyota huzaliwa wingu la gesi na vumbi (nebula) linapoanguka kwa mvutano. Mwisho wake hutegemea wingi: ndogo hufifia polepole, kubwa sana hulipuka kama supernova."),
   (["Birth: nebula collapses, heats up, and starts fusion → a star.", "Sun-like stars (about 10 billion years): swell into a red giant, shed their outer layers, and leave a white dwarf.", "Very massive stars: end in a supernova, leaving a neutron star or a black hole.", "Elements heavier than iron, and much of the carbon, oxygen and iron in our bodies, were made in stars and supernovae."],
    ["Naissance : la nébuleuse s'effondre, chauffe et démarre la fusion → une étoile.", "Étoiles comme le Soleil (environ 10 milliards d'années) : gonflent en géante rouge, rejettent leurs couches externes et laissent une naine blanche.", "Étoiles très massives : finissent en supernova, laissant une étoile à neutrons ou un trou noir.", "Les éléments lourds, et une grande partie du carbone, de l'oxygène et du fer de notre corps, ont été fabriqués dans les étoiles et les supernovae."],
    ["Kuvuka: nebula irasenyuka, igashyuha, igatangira fusion → inyenyeri.", "Inyenyeri nk'izuba (nka miliyari 10 z'imyaka): ziraraba zikaba red giants, zigata ibice byazo by'inyuma zigasiga white dwarf.", "Inyenyeri nini cyane: zirangirira muri supernova, zigasiga neutron star cyangwa black hole.", "Ibintu biremereye, n'ibice byinshi bya carbone, oxygen na fer biri mu mibiri yacu, byakozwe mu nyenyeri no muri supernovae."],
    ["Kuzaliwa: nebula huanguka, hupata joto, na kuanza muunganiko → nyota.", "Nyota kama Jua (takriban miaka bilioni 10): huvimba kuwa red giant, hutupa tabaka za nje na kuacha white dwarf.", "Nyota kubwa sana: huishia kwenye supernova, na kuacha neutron star au black hole.", "Elementi nzito, na sehemu kubwa ya kaboni, oksijeni na chuma mwilini mwetu, zilitengenezwa kwenye nyota na supernova."])),

_e("black_holes", ["stars_life_cycle", "universe_expansion"],
   ("What is a black hole?", "Qu'est-ce qu'un trou noir ?", "Black hole ni iki?", "Black hole ni nini?"),
   ("black hole|what is a black hole|event horizon|singularity|how do black holes form|supermassive black hole|can light escape a black hole|sagittarius a|neutron star vs black hole|wormhole",
    "trou noir|qu'est-ce qu'un trou noir|horizon des evenements|singularite|comment se forment les trous noirs|trou noir supermassif|la lumiere peut-elle s'echapper d'un trou noir|sagittarius a|trou de ver",
    "black hole|black hole ni iki|event horizon|singularity|black holes ziva he|supermassive black hole|urumuri rushobora gucika muri black hole|sagittarius a",
    "black hole|black hole ni nini|event horizon|singularity|black hole huundwaje|supermassive black hole|mwanga unaweza kutoroka black hole|sagittarius a"),
   ("A black hole is a region where gravity is so strong that nothing, not even light, can escape once it crosses the boundary called the event horizon. Many form when a very massive star collapses at the end of its life. Supermassive black holes, millions to billions of times the Sun's mass, sit at the centre of most large galaxies.",
    "Un trou noir est une région où la gravité est si forte que rien, pas même la lumière, ne peut s'en échapper une fois franchie la limite appelée horizon des événements. Beaucoup se forment quand une étoile très massive s'effondre à la fin de sa vie. Des trous noirs supermassifs, de millions à milliards de fois la masse du Soleil, se trouvent au centre de la plupart des grandes galaxies.",
    "Black hole ni agace aho gravity ikomeye cyane ku buryo nta kintu, ndetse n'urumuri, gishobora gusohoka iyo kirenze umupaka witwa event horizon. Nyinshi ziravuka iyo inyenyeri nini cyane isenyutse iyo irangije ubuzima. Supermassive black holes, ziruta izuba incuro miliyoni kugeza kuri miliyari, ziba hagati muri galaxies nini nyinshi.",
    "Black hole ni eneo ambapo mvutano una nguvu sana hata hakuna kitu, hata mwanga, kinaweza kutoroka kikishavuka mpaka unaoitwa event horizon. Nyingi huundwa nyota kubwa sana inapoanguka mwishoni mwa maisha yake. Supermassive black holes, mara milioni hadi bilioni ya uzito wa Jua, hukaa katikati ya galaksi nyingi kubwa."),
   (["In 2019 the Event Horizon Telescope published the first image of a black hole's shadow (in galaxy M87); in 2022 it imaged the one at the Milky Way's centre, Sagittarius A*.", "A black hole is not a cosmic vacuum cleaner: at a distance, its gravity acts like any object of the same mass.", "We detect them through their effect on nearby stars, hot glowing gas, and gravitational waves.", "Inside the event horizon our physics is incomplete; what happens at the centre (the singularity) is unknown."],
    ["En 2019 l'Event Horizon Telescope a publié la première image de l'ombre d'un trou noir (galaxie M87) ; en 2022, celle du centre de la Voie lactée, Sagittarius A*.", "Un trou noir n'est pas un aspirateur cosmique : à distance, sa gravité agit comme celle de tout objet de même masse.", "On les détecte par leur effet sur les étoiles voisines, le gaz chaud lumineux et les ondes gravitationnelles.", "À l'intérieur de l'horizon, notre physique est incomplète ; ce qui se passe au centre (la singularité) est inconnu."],
    ["Mu 2019 Event Horizon Telescope yatangaje ifoto ya mbere y'igicucu cya black hole (galaxy M87); mu 2022 yafashe iy'i hagati ya Milky Way, Sagittarius A*.", "Black hole si icyuma gikurura byose: iyo uri kure, gravity yayo ikora nk'iy'ikintu cyose gifite ubwinshi bumwe.", "Tuzibona binyuze ku ngaruka ku nyenyeri zegereye, imyuka ishyushye irabagirana, na gravitational waves.", "Imbere ya event horizon physics yacu ntirarangira; ibibera hagati (singularity) ntibizwi."],
    ["Mwaka 2019 Event Horizon Telescope ilitoa picha ya kwanza ya kivuli cha black hole (galaksi M87); 2022 ya katikati ya Milky Way, Sagittarius A*.", "Black hole si kisafishaji cha anga: ukiwa mbali, mvutano wake hufanya kama wa kitu chochote chenye wingi sawa.", "Tunaigundua kupitia athari kwa nyota za karibu, gesi moto inayong'aa, na mawimbi ya mvutano.", "Ndani ya event horizon fizikia yetu haijakamilika; yanayotokea katikati (singularity) hayajulikani."])),

_e("solar_system_formation", ["planets_overview", "earth_formation", "big_bang"],
   ("How was the Solar System formed?", "Comment le Système solaire s'est-il formé ?", "Sisitemu y'izuba yaremwe ite?", "Mfumo wa Jua uliundwaje?"),
   ("how was the solar system formed|formation of the solar system|origin of the solar system|how old is the solar system|solar nebula|how did the sun form|origin of the sun|how were planets formed|protoplanetary disk|age of the sun",
    "comment le systeme solaire s'est-il forme|formation du systeme solaire|origine du systeme solaire|age du systeme solaire|nebuleuse solaire|comment le soleil s'est-il forme|origine du soleil|comment les planetes se sont formees|disque protoplanetaire|age du soleil",
    "sisitemu y'izuba yaremwe ite|ishingwa rya sisitemu y'izuba|inkomoko ya sisitemu y'izuba|imyaka ya sisitemu y'izuba|izuba ryaremwe rite|inkomoko y'izuba|imibumbe yaremwe ite|imyaka y'izuba",
    "mfumo wa jua uliundwaje|kuundwa kwa mfumo wa jua|asili ya mfumo wa jua|umri wa mfumo wa jua|jua liliundwaje|asili ya jua|sayari ziliundwaje|umri wa jua"),
   ("About 4.6 billion years ago a cloud of gas and dust (the solar nebula) collapsed under gravity. Most material fell to the centre and became the Sun (about 99.8% of the system's mass). The rest flattened into a spinning disk where dust clumped into rocks, then planetesimals, then planets.",
    "Il y a environ 4,6 milliards d'années, un nuage de gaz et de poussière (la nébuleuse solaire) s'est effondré sous la gravité. L'essentiel de la matière est tombé au centre et a formé le Soleil (environ 99,8 % de la masse du système). Le reste s'est aplati en un disque en rotation où la poussière s'est agglomérée en roches, puis en planétésimaux, puis en planètes.",
    "Hashize imyaka nka miliyari 4.6 igicu cy'imyuka n'ivumbi (solar nebula) cyarasenyutse kubera gravity. Ibintu byinshi byagiye hagati bikaba izuba (nka 99.8% by'ubwinshi bwa sisitemu). Ibisigaye byahinduwe agafuka kazunguruka aho ivumbi ryafatanye rikaba amabuye, hanyuma planetesimals, hanyuma imibumbe.",
    "Takriban miaka bilioni 4.6 iliyopita wingu la gesi na vumbi (solar nebula) lilianguka kwa mvutano. Mada nyingi ilienda katikati na kuwa Jua (takriban 99.8% ya uzito wa mfumo). Iliyobaki ilitandazwa kuwa diski inayozunguka ambapo vumbi lilishikana kuwa miamba, kisha planetesimals, kisha sayari."),
   (["Near the Sun it was hot, so only rock and metal could solidify: the rocky planets Mercury, Venus, Earth and Mars.", "Farther out, ice also survived, so planets grew huge and gathered gas: Jupiter and Saturn (gas giants), Uranus and Neptune (ice giants).", "Evidence: all planets orbit in the same direction and nearly the same plane; meteorites date to about 4.57 billion years.", "Leftovers form the asteroid belt, comets and the Kuiper belt."],
    ["Près du Soleil il faisait chaud : seuls roche et métal ont pu se solidifier → planètes rocheuses Mercure, Vénus, Terre et Mars.", "Plus loin, la glace a aussi survécu : planètes géantes qui ont capté du gaz, Jupiter et Saturne (géantes gazeuses), Uranus et Neptune (géantes de glaces).", "Preuves : toutes les planètes tournent dans le même sens et presque dans le même plan ; les météorites datent d'environ 4,57 milliards d'années.", "Les restes forment la ceinture d'astéroïdes, les comètes et la ceinture de Kuiper."],
    ["Hafi y'izuba hari hashyushye: amabuye n'ibyuma gusa nibyo byashoboye gukomera → imibumbe y'amabuye Mercury, Venus, Isi na Mars.", "Kure, urubura na rwo rwarokotse: imibumbe minini yakusanyije imyuka, Jupiter na Saturn (gas giants), Uranus na Neptune (ice giants).", "Ibimenyetso: imibumbe yose izenguruka mu cyerekezo kimwe n'urwego rumwe; meteorites zifite imyaka nka miliyari 4.57.", "Ibisigaye bigize asteroid belt, comets na Kuiper belt."],
    ["Karibu na Jua palikuwa na joto: miamba na metali tu ndizo zilizoweza kuganda → sayari za miamba Zebaki, Zuhura, Dunia na Mirihi.", "Mbali zaidi barafu pia ilibaki: sayari kubwa zilikusanya gesi, Jupita na Zohali (gas giants), Uranus na Neptune (ice giants).", "Ushahidi: sayari zote huzunguka upande mmoja na karibu ndege moja; vimondo vina umri wa takriban miaka bilioni 4.57.", "Mabaki huunda ukanda wa asteroidi, nyotamkia na ukanda wa Kuiper."])),

_e("planets_overview", ["solar_system_formation", "earth_formation", "moon_formation"],
   ("What are the planets of the Solar System, in order?", "Quelles sont les planètes du Système solaire, dans l'ordre ?", "Imibumbe ya sisitemu y'izuba ni iyihe, ikurikirana ite?", "Sayari za Mfumo wa Jua ni zipi, kwa mpangilio?"),
   ("planets of the solar system|list of planets|eight planets|order of the planets|how many planets are there|is pluto a planet|dwarf planet|biggest planet|smallest planet|which planet is closest to the sun|hottest planet",
    "planetes du systeme solaire|liste des planetes|huit planetes|ordre des planetes|combien de planetes|pluton est-elle une planete|planete naine|plus grande planete|plus petite planete|planete la plus proche du soleil|planete la plus chaude",
    "imibumbe ya sisitemu y'izuba|urutonde rw'imibumbe|imibumbe umunani|imibumbe ni ingahe|pluto ni umubumbe|dwarf planet|umubumbe munini|umubumbe muto|umubumbe uri hafi y'izuba|umubumbe ushyushye cyane",
    "sayari za mfumo wa jua|orodha ya sayari|sayari nane|mpangilio wa sayari|kuna sayari ngapi|pluto ni sayari|sayari kibete|sayari kubwa zaidi|sayari ndogo zaidi|sayari iliyo karibu na jua|sayari yenye joto zaidi"),
   ("The Solar System has eight planets. In order from the Sun: Mercury, Venus, Earth, Mars, Jupiter, Saturn, Uranus, Neptune. The four inner planets are rocky; Jupiter and Saturn are gas giants; Uranus and Neptune are ice giants. In 2006 the International Astronomical Union reclassified Pluto as a dwarf planet.",
    "Le Système solaire compte huit planètes. Dans l'ordre à partir du Soleil : Mercure, Vénus, Terre, Mars, Jupiter, Saturne, Uranus, Neptune. Les quatre internes sont rocheuses ; Jupiter et Saturne sont des géantes gazeuses ; Uranus et Neptune des géantes de glaces. En 2006, l'Union astronomique internationale a reclassé Pluton en planète naine.",
    "Sisitemu y'izuba ifite imibumbe umunani. Uhereye ku zuba: Mercury, Venus, Isi, Mars, Jupiter, Saturn, Uranus, Neptune. Ine z'imbere ni iz'amabuye; Jupiter na Saturn ni gas giants; Uranus na Neptune ni ice giants. Mu 2006 International Astronomical Union yashyize Pluto mu cyiciro cya dwarf planet.",
    "Mfumo wa Jua una sayari nane. Kwa mpangilio kutoka Jua: Zebaki (Mercury), Zuhura (Venus), Dunia, Mirihi (Mars), Jupita, Zohali (Saturn), Uranus, Neptune. Nne za ndani ni za miamba; Jupita na Zohali ni gas giants; Uranus na Neptune ni ice giants. Mwaka 2006 Umoja wa Kimataifa wa Astronomia uliiainisha Pluto kuwa sayari kibete."),
   (["Mnemonic: My Very Educated Mother Just Served Us Noodles.", "Biggest: Jupiter (more than 1,300 Earths could fit inside). Smallest: Mercury. Hottest: Venus (about 465 °C, thick carbon-dioxide atmosphere).", "Saturn has the most visible rings; Mars has the tallest volcano, Olympus Mons; Venus spins backwards.", "One Earth year ≈ 365.25 days; a year on Mars ≈ 687 Earth days; on Neptune ≈ 165 Earth years."],
    ["Moyen mnémotechnique (en anglais) : My Very Educated Mother Just Served Us Noodles.", "Plus grande : Jupiter (plus de 1 300 Terres y tiendraient). Plus petite : Mercure. Plus chaude : Vénus (environ 465 °C, épaisse atmosphère de CO₂).", "Saturne a les anneaux les plus visibles ; Mars a le plus haut volcan, Olympus Mons ; Vénus tourne à l'envers.", "Une année terrestre ≈ 365,25 jours ; une année sur Mars ≈ 687 jours terrestres ; sur Neptune ≈ 165 ans terrestres."],
    ["Uburyo bwo kwibuka (mu cyongereza): My Very Educated Mother Just Served Us Noodles.", "Nini: Jupiter (Isi irenga 1,300 zagwamo). Nto: Mercury. Ishyushye: Venus (nka 465 °C, umwuka mwinshi wa CO₂).", "Saturn ifite impeta zigaragara cyane; Mars ifite ikirunga kirekire, Olympus Mons; Venus izunguruka inyuma.", "Umwaka umwe w'Isi ≈ iminsi 365.25; umwaka kuri Mars ≈ iminsi 687; kuri Neptune ≈ imyaka 165 y'Isi."],
    ["Njia ya kukumbuka (kwa Kiingereza): My Very Educated Mother Just Served Us Noodles.", "Kubwa: Jupita (zaidi ya Dunia 1,300 zingeingia ndani). Ndogo: Zebaki. Yenye joto zaidi: Zuhura (takriban 465 °C, angahewa nene ya CO₂).", "Zohali ina pete zinazoonekana zaidi; Mirihi ina volkano ndefu zaidi, Olympus Mons; Zuhura huzunguka kinyume.", "Mwaka mmoja wa Dunia ≈ siku 365.25; mwaka Mirihi ≈ siku 687 za Dunia; Neptune ≈ miaka 165 ya Dunia."])),

_e("earth_formation", ["solar_system_formation", "moon_formation", "origin_of_life", "plate_tectonics"],
   ("How was the Earth formed and how old is it?", "Comment la Terre s'est-elle formée et quel âge a-t-elle ?", "Isi yaremwe ite kandi ifite imyaka ingahe?", "Dunia iliundwaje na ina umri gani?"),
   ("how was the earth formed|how old is the earth|age of the earth|formation of the earth|origin of the earth|history of the earth|how did earth form|geological time scale|layers of the earth|earth's core",
    "comment la terre s'est-elle formee|quel age a la terre|age de la terre|formation de la terre|origine de la terre|histoire de la terre|echelle des temps geologiques|couches de la terre|noyau de la terre",
    "isi yaremwe ite|isi ifite imyaka ingahe|imyaka y'isi|ishingwa ry'isi|inkomoko y'isi|amateka y'isi|ibice by'isi|umutima w'isi",
    "dunia iliundwaje|dunia ina umri gani|umri wa dunia|kuundwa kwa dunia|asili ya dunia|historia ya dunia|tabaka za dunia|kiini cha dunia"),
   ("Earth formed about 4.54 billion years ago as dust and rock in the young Sun's disk collided and merged. It started molten; heavy iron sank to form the core while lighter rock formed the mantle and thin crust. Its age comes from radiometric dating of the oldest meteorites and Earth rocks.",
    "La Terre s'est formée il y a environ 4,54 milliards d'années, quand poussières et roches du disque du jeune Soleil sont entrées en collision et ont fusionné. Elle était d'abord en fusion ; le fer lourd a coulé pour former le noyau tandis que la roche plus légère formait le manteau et la fine croûte. Son âge vient de la datation radiométrique des plus vieilles météorites et roches terrestres.",
    "Isi yaremwe hashize imyaka nka miliyari 4.54 ubwo ivumbi n'amabuye byo mu gafuka k'izuba rito byagonganaga bigahurira hamwe. Mbere yari mu mazi ashyushye; icyuma kiremereye cyarimbutse gikora core, naho amabuye yoroshye akora mantle na crust yoroheje. Imyaka yayo ibarwa hakoreshejwe radiometric dating ku meteorites za kera n'amabuye y'Isi.",
    "Dunia iliundwa takriban miaka bilioni 4.54 iliyopita vumbi na miamba ya diski ya Jua changa yalipogongana na kuungana. Mwanzoni ilikuwa kioevu moto; chuma kizito kilizama kuunda kiini huku miamba myepesi ikaunda mantle na ganda jembamba. Umri wake hutoka kwenye upimaji wa radiometric wa vimondo vya kale na miamba ya Dunia."),
   (["Layers: inner core (solid iron-nickel), outer core (liquid), mantle (hot, slowly flowing rock), crust (thin outer shell).", "The Hadean eon (4.54–4.0 billion years ago) was hot and violent; oceans formed once it cooled enough, probably before 4.2 billion years ago.", "Oldest known mineral crystals (zircons from Australia) are about 4.4 billion years old.", "Timeline: Precambrian (about 88% of Earth's history) → Paleozoic → Mesozoic (dinosaurs) → Cenozoic (mammals, humans)."],
    ["Couches : noyau interne (fer-nickel solide), noyau externe (liquide), manteau (roche chaude qui flue lentement), croûte (fine enveloppe externe).", "L'Hadéen (4,54–4,0 milliards d'années) était chaud et violent ; les océans se sont formés dès que la surface a assez refroidi, probablement avant 4,2 milliards d'années.", "Les plus vieux cristaux connus (zircons d'Australie) ont environ 4,4 milliards d'années.", "Chronologie : Précambrien (environ 88 % de l'histoire de la Terre) → Paléozoïque → Mésozoïque (dinosaures) → Cénozoïque (mammifères, humains)."],
    ["Ibice: core y'imbere (icyuma-nickel gikomeye), core yo hanze (amazi), mantle (amabuye ashyushye atemba buhoro), crust (igikonjo cyoroheje cyo hanze).", "Hadean (miliyari 4.54–4.0) hari hashyushye kandi hahangayikishije; inyanja zaje hakonje bihagije, birashoboka mbere ya miliyari 4.2.", "Kristali za kera zizwi (zircons zo muri Australia) zifite imyaka nka miliyari 4.4.", "Igihe: Precambrian (nka 88% by'amateka y'Isi) → Paleozoic → Mesozoic (dinosaurs) → Cenozoic (inyamabere, abantu)."],
    ["Tabaka: kiini cha ndani (chuma-nikeli kigumu), kiini cha nje (kioevu), mantle (mwamba moto unaotiririka polepole), ganda (ganda jembamba la nje).", "Hadean (miaka bilioni 4.54–4.0) ilikuwa na joto na vurugu; bahari ziliundwa ilipopoa vya kutosha, pengine kabla ya miaka bilioni 4.2.", "Fuwele za kale zaidi zinazojulikana (zircons za Australia) zina umri wa takriban miaka bilioni 4.4.", "Ratiba: Precambrian (takriban 88% ya historia ya Dunia) → Paleozoic → Mesozoic (dinosauri) → Cenozoic (mamalia, binadamu)."])),

_e("moon_formation", ["earth_formation", "planets_overview"],
   ("How was the Moon formed?", "Comment la Lune s'est-elle formée ?", "Ukwezi cyaremwe gite?", "Mwezi uliundwaje?"),
   ("how was the moon formed|formation of the moon|origin of the moon|giant impact hypothesis|theia|why does the moon have phases|moon landing|how far is the moon|moon facts|first man on the moon",
    "comment la lune s'est-elle formee|formation de la lune|origine de la lune|hypothese de l'impact geant|theia|pourquoi la lune a-t-elle des phases|alunissage|distance de la lune|faits sur la lune|premier homme sur la lune",
    "ukwezi cyaremwe gite|ishingwa ry'ukwezi|inkomoko y'ukwezi|giant impact|theia|kuki ukwezi kugira amaboko|kugwa ku kwezi|intera y'ukwezi|umuntu wa mbere ku kwezi",
    "mwezi uliundwaje|kuundwa kwa mwezi|asili ya mwezi|giant impact|theia|kwa nini mwezi una awamu|kutua mwezini|umbali wa mwezi|mtu wa kwanza mwezini"),
   ("The leading explanation is the giant-impact hypothesis: about 4.5 billion years ago a Mars-sized body, often called Theia, struck the young Earth. The debris orbited Earth and clumped together to form the Moon. Moon rocks brought back by Apollo match Earth's mantle in composition, supporting this.",
    "L'explication dominante est l'hypothèse de l'impact géant : il y a environ 4,5 milliards d'années, un corps de la taille de Mars, souvent appelé Théia, a percuté la jeune Terre. Les débris ont orbité autour de la Terre puis se sont agglomérés pour former la Lune. Les roches lunaires rapportées par Apollo ont une composition proche du manteau terrestre, ce qui appuie cette hypothèse.",
    "Ibisobanuro bikomeye ni giant-impact hypothesis: hashize imyaka nka miliyari 4.5 igikoko gifite ubunini bwa Mars, kenshi cyitwa Theia, cyagonze Isi nto. Ibisigazwa byazengurutse Isi bikomatana bikora Ukwezi. Amabuye y'ukwezi yazanwe na Apollo ahuje n'ay'Isi mu miterere, bikemeza ibi.",
    "Maelezo makuu ni giant-impact hypothesis: takriban miaka bilioni 4.5 iliyopita kitu chenye ukubwa wa Mirihi, mara nyingi huitwa Theia, kiligonga Dunia changa. Vipande vilizunguka Dunia na kuungana kuunda Mwezi. Miamba ya mwezi iliyoletwa na Apollo inafanana na mantle ya Dunia, ikiunga mkono nadharia hii."),
   (["The Moon is about 384,400 km away and takes about 27.3 days to orbit Earth.", "Phases happen because we see different amounts of its sunlit half as it orbits; the Moon makes no light of its own.", "Neil Armstrong was the first person to walk on the Moon, on 20 July 1969 (Apollo 11).", "The Moon drifts away from Earth by about 3.8 cm each year and causes ocean tides."],
    ["La Lune est à environ 384 400 km et met environ 27,3 jours pour tourner autour de la Terre.", "Les phases viennent de la part variable de sa moitié éclairée que nous voyons ; la Lune ne produit pas de lumière.", "Neil Armstrong fut le premier homme à marcher sur la Lune, le 20 juillet 1969 (Apollo 11).", "La Lune s'éloigne de la Terre d'environ 3,8 cm par an et provoque les marées."],
    ["Ukwezi kiri ku ntera ya km 384,400 kandi kimara iminsi nka 27.3 kizenguruka Isi.", "Amaboko y'ukwezi avuka kuko tubona ibice bitandukanye by'igice cyaka; ukwezi nticyikorera urumuri.", "Neil Armstrong niwe muntu wa mbere wagenze ku kwezi, ku wa 20 Nyakanga 1969 (Apollo 11).", "Ukwezi kirimo kuva ku Isi nka cm 3.8 buri mwaka kandi gitera imivumba y'inyanja (tides)."],
    ["Mwezi uko umbali wa km 384,400 na huchukua takriban siku 27.3 kuzunguka Dunia.", "Awamu hutokea kwa sababu tunaona kiasi tofauti cha nusu yake iliyoangaziwa; Mwezi hauzalishi mwanga wake.", "Neil Armstrong alikuwa mtu wa kwanza kutembea mwezini, tarehe 20 Julai 1969 (Apollo 11).", "Mwezi hujiondoa kutoka Dunia takriban cm 3.8 kila mwaka na husababisha mawimbi ya bahari."])),

_e("origin_of_life", ["earth_formation", "evolution_darwin", "dinosaur_extinction"],
   ("How did life begin on Earth?", "Comment la vie a-t-elle commencé sur Terre ?", "Ubuzima bwatangiye bute ku Isi?", "Uhai ulianzaje duniani?"),
   ("how did life begin|origin of life|first life on earth|abiogenesis|first living things|how life started|primordial soup|oldest fossils|cambrian explosion|great oxidation event",
    "comment la vie a-t-elle commence|origine de la vie|premiere vie sur terre|abiogenese|premiers etres vivants|comment la vie a demarre|soupe primitive|plus vieux fossiles|explosion cambrienne|grande oxydation",
    "ubuzima bwatangiye bute|inkomoko y'ubuzima|ubuzima bwa mbere ku isi|abiogenesis|ibinyabuzima bya mbere|fosili za kera|cambrian explosion|great oxidation",
    "uhai ulianzaje|asili ya uhai|uhai wa kwanza duniani|abiogenesis|viumbe vya kwanza|mafuta ya kale ya viumbe|visukuku vya kale|cambrian explosion|great oxidation"),
   ("Nobody knows exactly how life began, but the leading idea (abiogenesis) is that simple organic molecules in early oceans or hot vents gradually became self-copying systems. The earliest widely accepted evidence of life is about 3.5 billion years old, microbial mats and stromatolites. For most of Earth's history life was microscopic.",
    "Personne ne sait exactement comment la vie a commencé, mais l'idée dominante (abiogenèse) est que de simples molécules organiques des premiers océans ou sources hydrothermales sont devenues peu à peu des systèmes capables de se copier. La plus ancienne preuve largement admise date d'environ 3,5 milliards d'années : tapis microbiens et stromatolithes. Pendant l'essentiel de l'histoire de la Terre, la vie était microscopique.",
    "Nta n'umwe uzi neza uko ubuzima bwatangiye, ariko igitekerezo gikomeye (abiogenesis) ni uko molekile zoroheje zo mu nyanja za mbere cyangwa mu byuma bishyushye zagiye zihinduka sisitemu zishobora kwikopera. Ikimenyetso cyizewe cyane gifite imyaka nka miliyari 3.5, microbial mats na stromatolites. Igihe kinini cy'amateka y'Isi ubuzima bwari bito cyane.",
    "Hakuna anayejua hasa jinsi uhai ulivyoanza, lakini wazo kuu (abiogenesis) ni kuwa molekuli rahisi za kikaboni katika bahari za awali au matundu ya joto zilibadilika polepole kuwa mifumo inayojinakili. Ushahidi wa kale unaokubalika sana una umri wa takriban miaka bilioni 3.5, mikeka ya vijidudu na stromatolites. Kwa sehemu kubwa ya historia ya Dunia uhai ulikuwa wa hadubini."),
   (["About 2.4 billion years ago: cyanobacteria made oxygen by photosynthesis (the Great Oxidation Event), changing the atmosphere.", "About 1.5–2 billion years ago: complex cells (eukaryotes) appeared; later, multicellular life.", "About 540 million years ago: the Cambrian explosion, a rapid diversification of animal groups.", "About 470 million years ago: plants moved onto land; about 375 million years ago: the first four-legged animals."],
    ["Il y a environ 2,4 milliards d'années : les cyanobactéries produisent de l'oxygène par photosynthèse (la Grande oxydation), ce qui change l'atmosphère.", "Il y a environ 1,5–2 milliards d'années : cellules complexes (eucaryotes) ; plus tard, la vie pluricellulaire.", "Il y a environ 540 millions d'années : l'explosion cambrienne, diversification rapide des groupes animaux.", "Il y a environ 470 millions d'années : les plantes conquièrent la terre ; il y a environ 375 millions d'années : premiers animaux à quatre pattes."],
    ["Hashize imyaka nka miliyari 2.4: cyanobacteria zakoze oxygen binyuze muri photosynthesis (Great Oxidation Event), bihindura umwuka.", "Hashize imyaka nka miliyari 1.5–2: ingirabuzimafatizo zikomeye (eukaryotes) zagaragaye; hanyuma ubuzima bw'ingirabuzimafatizo nyinshi.", "Hashize imyaka nka miliyoni 540: Cambrian explosion, kwiyongera vuba kw'amatsinda y'inyamaswa.", "Hashize imyaka nka miliyoni 470: ibimera byajya ku butaka; nka miliyoni 375: inyamaswa za mbere z'amaguru ane."],
    ["Takriban miaka bilioni 2.4 iliyopita: cyanobacteria zilizalisha oksijeni kwa usanisinuru (Great Oxidation Event), na kubadilisha angahewa.", "Takriban miaka bilioni 1.5–2 iliyopita: seli changamano (eukaryotes) zilitokea; baadaye uhai wa seli nyingi.", "Takriban miaka milioni 540 iliyopita: Cambrian explosion, kuongezeka kwa kasi kwa makundi ya wanyama.", "Takriban miaka milioni 470 iliyopita: mimea ilihamia nchi kavu; takriban miaka milioni 375: wanyama wa kwanza wenye miguu minne."])),

_e("plate_tectonics", ["earth_formation", "dinosaur_extinction"],
   ("What is plate tectonics and why do continents move? (earthquakes, volcanoes, Pangaea)", "Qu'est-ce que la tectonique des plaques ? (séismes, volcans, Pangée)", "Plate tectonics ni iki? (imitingito, ibirunga, Pangaea)", "Plate tectonics ni nini? (matetemeko, volkano, Pangaea)"),
   ("plate tectonics|continental drift|pangaea|why do continents move|what causes earthquakes|what causes volcanoes|tectonic plates|earthquake|volcano|rift valley|ring of fire",
    "tectonique des plaques|derive des continents|pangee|pourquoi les continents bougent|cause des seismes|cause des volcans|plaques tectoniques|tremblement de terre|volcan|rift|ceinture de feu",
    "plate tectonics|kwimuka kw'ibihugu|pangaea|kuki ibihugu byimuka|icyateye umutingito|icyateye ibirunga|plaques za tectonic|umutingito|ikirunga|rift valley|ring of fire",
    "plate tectonics|kuhama kwa mabara|pangaea|kwa nini mabara yanahama|nini husababisha matetemeko|nini husababisha volkano|bamba za tectonic|tetemeko la ardhi|volkano|bonde la ufa|ring of fire"),
   ("Earth's outer shell is broken into large plates that slowly move, a few centimetres a year, carried by heat-driven flow in the mantle. Where plates collide, slide past or pull apart we get mountains, earthquakes, volcanoes and rifts. Alfred Wegener proposed continental drift in 1912; plate tectonics was accepted in the 1960s.",
    "L'enveloppe externe de la Terre est fragmentée en grandes plaques qui se déplacent lentement, de quelques centimètres par an, entraînées par des courants de chaleur dans le manteau. Là où elles se heurtent, glissent ou s'écartent, apparaissent montagnes, séismes, volcans et rifts. Alfred Wegener a proposé la dérive des continents en 1912 ; la tectonique des plaques fut acceptée dans les années 1960.",
    "Igikonjo cy'inyuma cy'Isi cyacitsemo ibyuma binini (plates) bigenda buhoro, cm nke ku mwaka, bijyanywe n'imigendere y'ubushyuhe muri mantle. Aho zihurira, zinyuranamo cyangwa zitandukana habaho imisozi, imitingito, ibirunga na rifts. Alfred Wegener yatanze igitekerezo cya continental drift mu 1912; plate tectonics yemewe mu myaka ya 1960.",
    "Ganda la nje la Dunia limevunjika kuwa mabamba makubwa yanayosogea polepole, sentimita chache kwa mwaka, yakibebwa na mtiririko wa joto kwenye mantle. Yanapogongana, kuteleza au kutengana hutokea milima, matetemeko, volkano na mabonde ya ufa. Alfred Wegener alipendekeza continental drift mwaka 1912; plate tectonics ilikubaliwa miaka ya 1960."),
   (["About 335–175 million years ago the continents were joined as the supercontinent Pangaea; it split into today's continents.", "Collision: India hitting Asia built the Himalayas. Pulling apart: the East African Rift is slowly splitting Africa.", "Most earthquakes and volcanoes occur on plate boundaries, such as the 'Ring of Fire' around the Pacific.", "Evidence: matching coastlines and fossils across oceans, seafloor spreading, and GPS measurements of plate motion."],
    ["Il y a environ 335–175 millions d'années, les continents formaient le supercontinent Pangée ; il s'est fragmenté en continents actuels.", "Collision : l'Inde percutant l'Asie a formé l'Himalaya. Écartement : le rift est-africain sépare lentement l'Afrique.", "La plupart des séismes et volcans surviennent aux limites de plaques, comme la « ceinture de feu » du Pacifique.", "Preuves : côtes et fossiles qui s'emboîtent de part et d'autre des océans, expansion des fonds océaniques, mesures GPS."],
    ["Hashize imyaka miliyoni 335–175 ibihugu byari bifatanye nka Pangaea; yaje gucikamo ibihugu bya none.", "Kugongana: Ubuhinde bwagonze Aziya bukora Himalaya. Gutandukana: East African Rift irimo gutandukanya Afurika buhoro.", "Imitingito n'ibirunga byinshi biba ku mipaka ya plates, nka «Ring of Fire» y'inyanja ya Pacific.", "Ibimenyetso: inkombe n'ibisigazwa bihuye hakurya y'inyanja, seafloor spreading, n'ibipimo bya GPS."],
    ["Takriban miaka milioni 335–175 iliyopita mabara yalikuwa yameungana kama Pangaea; ilivunjika kuwa mabara ya leo.", "Mgongano: India kugonga Asia kuliunda Himalaya. Kutengana: Bonde la Ufa la Afrika Mashariki linagawanya Afrika polepole.", "Matetemeko na volkano nyingi hutokea kwenye mipaka ya mabamba, kama 'Ring of Fire' ya Pasifiki.", "Ushahidi: pwani na visukuku vinavyolingana kuvuka bahari, seafloor spreading, na vipimo vya GPS."])),

_e("dinosaur_extinction", ["plate_tectonics", "evolution_darwin", "origin_of_life"],
   ("When did dinosaurs live and why did they go extinct?", "Quand vivaient les dinosaures et pourquoi ont-ils disparu ?", "Dinosaurs babayeho ryari kandi kuki bashize?", "Dinosauri waliishi lini na kwa nini walitoweka?"),
   ("dinosaurs|when did dinosaurs live|why did dinosaurs go extinct|dinosaur extinction|chicxulub|asteroid impact|mass extinction|permian extinction|t rex|fossils",
    "dinosaures|quand vivaient les dinosaures|pourquoi les dinosaures ont-ils disparu|extinction des dinosaures|chicxulub|impact d'asteroide|extinction de masse|extinction permienne|t rex|fossiles",
    "dinosaurs|dinosaurs babayeho ryari|kuki dinosaurs bashize|kuzimira kwa dinosaurs|chicxulub|asteroid|kuzimira kwinshi|t rex|fosili",
    "dinosauri|dinosauri waliishi lini|kwa nini dinosauri walitoweka|kutoweka kwa dinosauri|chicxulub|asteroidi|kutoweka kwa wingi|t rex|visukuku"),
   ("Non-bird dinosaurs lived from about 230 to 66 million years ago (the Mesozoic Era). Most scientists conclude that they died out 66 million years ago mainly because a large asteroid, about 10 km wide, struck near Chicxulub in Mexico, causing global fires, darkness and climate collapse; huge volcanic eruptions (Deccan Traps) probably added stress. Birds are living descendants of small feathered dinosaurs.",
    "Les dinosaures non aviens ont vécu d'environ 230 à 66 millions d'années (l'ère mésozoïque). La plupart des scientifiques concluent qu'ils ont disparu il y a 66 millions d'années surtout à cause d'un grand astéroïde d'environ 10 km qui a frappé près de Chicxulub (Mexique), causant incendies, obscurité et effondrement du climat ; d'énormes éruptions volcaniques (trapps du Deccan) ont probablement aggravé la situation. Les oiseaux descendent de petits dinosaures à plumes.",
    "Dinosaurs zitari inyoni zabayeho kuva hashize imyaka miliyoni 230 kugeza kuri 66 (Mesozoic Era). Abahanga benshi basanga zarashize hashize imyaka miliyoni 66 cyane cyane kubera asteroid nini, ubugari bwa km 10, yagonze hafi ya Chicxulub muri Mexique, ikazana inkongi, umwijima no kwangirika kw'ikirere; ibirunga binini (Deccan Traps) bishobora kuba byarongeyeho. Inyoni ni abakomoka kuri dinosaurs ntoya zifite amababa.",
    "Dinosauri wasio ndege waliishi takriban miaka milioni 230 hadi 66 iliyopita (Enzi ya Mesozoic). Wanasayansi wengi wanahitimisha walitoweka miaka milioni 66 iliyopita hasa kwa asteroidi kubwa ya takriban km 10 iliyogonga karibu na Chicxulub, Mexico, ikisababisha moto, giza na kuvurugika kwa hali ya hewa; milipuko mikubwa ya volkano (Deccan Traps) huenda iliongeza shinikizo. Ndege ni wazao hai wa dinosauri wadogo wenye manyoya."),
   (["Mesozoic periods: Triassic, Jurassic, Cretaceous. T. rex lived in the late Cretaceous, near the end.", "Evidence: a worldwide thin layer rich in iridium (found by Alvarez, 1980) and the buried Chicxulub crater.", "About 75% of species vanished in this mass extinction, which opened space for mammals to diversify.", "Earth has had five major mass extinctions; the worst, about 252 million years ago (end-Permian), killed over 90% of marine species."],
    ["Périodes du Mésozoïque : Trias, Jurassique, Crétacé. Le T. rex vivait à la fin du Crétacé.", "Preuves : une fine couche mondiale riche en iridium (Alvarez, 1980) et le cratère enfoui de Chicxulub.", "Environ 75 % des espèces ont disparu lors de cette extinction, ce qui a laissé de la place aux mammifères.", "La Terre a connu cinq grandes extinctions ; la pire, il y a environ 252 millions d'années (fin du Permien), a tué plus de 90 % des espèces marines."],
    ["Ibihe bya Mesozoic: Triassic, Jurassic, Cretaceous. T. rex yabayeho mu mpera ya Cretaceous.", "Ibimenyetso: igice cyoroheje ku isi hose gifite iridium nyinshi (Alvarez, 1980) n'icyobo cya Chicxulub.", "Nka 75% by'amoko byarashize, bikaba byarahaye inyamabere umwanya wo gutandukana.", "Isi yagize kuzimira kwinshi gutanu; kubi cyane, hashize imyaka nka miliyoni 252 (end-Permian), kwishe amoko y'inyanja arenga 90%."],
    ["Vipindi vya Mesozoic: Triassic, Jurassic, Cretaceous. T. rex aliishi mwishoni mwa Cretaceous.", "Ushahidi: tabaka jembamba duniani kote lenye iridium nyingi (Alvarez, 1980) na kreta iliyofukiwa ya Chicxulub.", "Takriban 75% ya spishi zilipotea, na kuwapa mamalia nafasi ya kuongezeka.", "Dunia imekuwa na kutoweka kwa wingi mara tano; kubaya zaidi, takriban miaka milioni 252 iliyopita (end-Permian), kuliua zaidi ya 90% ya spishi za baharini."])),

_e("evolution_darwin", ["human_evolution", "origin_of_life", "dinosaur_extinction"],
   ("What is evolution and natural selection (Darwin)?", "Qu'est-ce que l'évolution et la sélection naturelle (Darwin) ?", "Evolution na natural selection (Darwin) ni iki?", "Mageuzi (evolution) na uteuzi asilia (Darwin) ni nini?"),
   ("evolution|theory of evolution|natural selection|charles darwin|origin of species|darwin|what is evolution|evidence for evolution|survival of the fittest|adaptation",
    "evolution|theorie de l'evolution|selection naturelle|charles darwin|l'origine des especes|darwin|qu'est-ce que l'evolution|preuves de l'evolution|survie du plus apte|adaptation",
    "evolution|theory ya evolution|natural selection|charles darwin|inkomoko y'amoko|darwin|evolution ni iki|ibimenyetso bya evolution|adaptation",
    "mageuzi|nadharia ya mageuzi|uteuzi asilia|charles darwin|asili ya spishi|darwin|mageuzi ni nini|ushahidi wa mageuzi|kuishi kwa aliye bora|kujirekebisha"),
   ("Evolution is the change in the inherited traits of living populations over generations. Charles Darwin (On the Origin of Species, 1859) explained its main mechanism, natural selection: individuals vary, some variations help them survive and reproduce better, and those traits become more common over time. All life shares common ancestry.",
    "L'évolution est le changement, au fil des générations, des caractères héréditaires des populations vivantes. Charles Darwin (De l'origine des espèces, 1859) en a expliqué le mécanisme principal, la sélection naturelle : les individus varient, certaines variations aident à mieux survivre et se reproduire, et ces caractères deviennent plus fréquents. Tous les êtres vivants ont des ancêtres communs.",
    "Evolution ni uguhinduka kw'imiterere ikomoka ku babyeyi mu moko y'ibinyabuzima uko ibisekuru bikurikirana. Charles Darwin (On the Origin of Species, 1859) yasobanuye uburyo bukuru, natural selection: ibinyabuzima biratandukanye, bimwe mu bitandukanye bifasha kubaho no kororoka neza, bityo iyo miterere ikiyongera uko igihe gishira. Ibinyabuzima byose bifite abakurambere basangiye.",
    "Mageuzi ni mabadiliko ya sifa za kurithi za idadi ya viumbe kwa vizazi. Charles Darwin (On the Origin of Species, 1859) alielezea utaratibu mkuu, uteuzi asilia: watu hutofautiana, tofauti zingine husaidia kuishi na kuzaa vizuri, na sifa hizo huongezeka kadri muda unavyopita. Viumbe vyote vina asili moja."),
   (["Evidence: the fossil record, DNA similarities (humans and chimpanzees share about 98–99% of coding DNA), shared anatomy such as limb bones, and observed change in bacteria and finches.", "Example: bacteria with resistance to an antibiotic survive treatment and multiply; resistance spreads.", "Evolution is a fact (change over time) and a theory (a tested, evidence-based explanation of how); 'theory' in science does not mean 'guess'.", "'Survival of the fittest' means best fitted to the environment, not the strongest; humans did not come from modern monkeys, both share an older ancestor."],
    ["Preuves : les fossiles, les ressemblances d'ADN (humains et chimpanzés partagent environ 98–99 % de l'ADN codant), l'anatomie commune comme les os des membres, et les changements observés chez les bactéries et les pinsons.", "Exemple : les bactéries résistantes à un antibiotique survivent au traitement et se multiplient ; la résistance se répand.", "L'évolution est un fait (changement dans le temps) et une théorie (explication testée appuyée sur des preuves) ; « théorie » en science ne veut pas dire « hypothèse ».", "« Survie du plus apte » signifie le mieux adapté au milieu, pas le plus fort ; l'homme ne descend pas des singes actuels, ils partagent un ancêtre plus ancien."],
    ["Ibimenyetso: fosili, ADN zisa (abantu na chimpanzees basangira nka 98–99% ya ADN), imiterere isa nk'amagufwa y'ingingo, n'impinduka zabonywe muri bagiteri n'inyoni.", "Urugero: bagiteri zirwanya antibiyotike zirarokoka zikiyongera; ubushobozi bwo kurwanya burakwirakwira.", "Evolution ni ukuri (impinduka uko igihe gishira) kandi ni theory (ibisobanuro byageragejwe bishingiye ku bimenyetso); 'theory' muri siyansi ntibivuga 'ikigereranyo'.", "'Survival of the fittest' bivuga uhuye neza n'ibidukikije, si ukomeye; abantu ntibakomoka ku nkende za none, basangiye umukurambere wa kera."],
    ["Ushahidi: visukuku, DNA zinazofanana (binadamu na sokwe hushiriki takriban 98–99% ya DNA), anatomia inayofanana kama mifupa ya viungo, na mabadiliko yaliyoonekana kwa bakteria na ndege.", "Mfano: bakteria sugu kwa antibiotiki huokoka matibabu na kuongezeka; usugu huenea.", "Mageuzi ni ukweli (mabadiliko kwa muda) na nadharia (maelezo yaliyojaribiwa yenye ushahidi); 'nadharia' katika sayansi haimaanishi 'dhana'.", "'Survival of the fittest' inamaanisha anayefaa zaidi mazingira, si mwenye nguvu zaidi; binadamu hakutokana na nyani wa leo, wanashiriki babu wa zamani."])),

_e("human_evolution", ["evolution_darwin", "agricultural_revolution", "origin_of_life"],
   ("Where and when did humans evolve?", "Où et quand les humains ont-ils évolué ?", "Abantu bavukiye he kandi ryari?", "Binadamu walibadilika wapi na lini?"),
   ("human evolution|origin of humans|where did humans come from|homo sapiens|neanderthals|lucy australopithecus|out of africa|first humans|homo erectus|stone age",
    "evolution humaine|origine des humains|d'ou viennent les humains|homo sapiens|neandertaliens|lucy australopitheque|sortie d'afrique|premiers humains|homo erectus|age de pierre",
    "evolution y'abantu|inkomoko y'abantu|abantu baturutse he|homo sapiens|neanderthals|lucy|abantu ba mbere|homo erectus|igihe cy'amabuye",
    "mageuzi ya binadamu|asili ya binadamu|binadamu walitoka wapi|homo sapiens|neanderthals|lucy|binadamu wa kwanza|homo erectus|enzi ya mawe"),
   ("Humans evolved in Africa. Our species, Homo sapiens, appeared there about 300,000 years ago (fossils from Jebel Irhoud, Morocco, and Ethiopia). Groups spread out of Africa, in major waves starting roughly 70,000–60,000 years ago, and reached Europe, Asia, Australia and later the Americas. Our lineage split from the ancestors of chimpanzees about 6–7 million years ago.",
    "Les humains ont évolué en Afrique. Notre espèce, Homo sapiens, y est apparue il y a environ 300 000 ans (fossiles de Jebel Irhoud, Maroc, et d'Éthiopie). Des groupes ont quitté l'Afrique, avec de grandes vagues à partir d'il y a environ 70 000–60 000 ans, et atteint l'Europe, l'Asie, l'Australie puis les Amériques. Notre lignée s'est séparée de celle des chimpanzés il y a environ 6 à 7 millions d'années.",
    "Abantu bavukiye muri Afurika. Ubwoko bwacu, Homo sapiens, bwagaragaye aho hashize imyaka nka 300,000 (fosili za Jebel Irhoud muri Maroc, no muri Etiyopiya). Amatsinda yavuye muri Afurika, mu mivumba minini guhera nka 70,000–60,000 ishize, agera i Burayi, Aziya, Australia, hanyuma muri Amerika. Umurongo wacu watandukanyije n'uw'ibisimba chimpanzees hashize imyaka nka miliyoni 6–7.",
    "Binadamu walibadilika Afrika. Spishi yetu, Homo sapiens, ilitokea huko takriban miaka 300,000 iliyopita (visukuku vya Jebel Irhoud, Moroko, na Ethiopia). Makundi yalitoka Afrika, kwa mawimbi makubwa kuanzia takriban miaka 70,000–60,000 iliyopita, na kufika Ulaya, Asia, Australia na baadaye Amerika. Ukoo wetu ulijitenga na sokwe takriban miaka milioni 6–7 iliyopita."),
   (["About 4–2 million years ago: Australopithecus walked upright; 'Lucy' (Ethiopia, about 3.2 million years old) is the famous skeleton.", "About 2.4–1.5 million years ago: Homo habilis made stone tools; Homo erectus (from about 1.9 million years ago) used fire and migrated beyond Africa.", "Neanderthals lived in Europe and western Asia until about 40,000 years ago; many people outside Africa carry about 1–2% Neanderthal DNA.", "About 40,000–10,000 years ago: cave art, burials, boats; then the move to farming."],
    ["Il y a environ 4 à 2 millions d'années : les australopithèques marchaient debout ; « Lucy » (Éthiopie, environ 3,2 millions d'années) est le squelette célèbre.", "Il y a environ 2,4 à 1,5 million d'années : Homo habilis fabrique des outils de pierre ; Homo erectus (dès environ 1,9 million d'années) utilise le feu et quitte l'Afrique.", "Les Néandertaliens vivaient en Europe et en Asie occidentale jusqu'à il y a environ 40 000 ans ; beaucoup de personnes hors d'Afrique portent 1 à 2 % d'ADN néandertalien.", "Il y a environ 40 000 à 10 000 ans : art rupestre, sépultures, bateaux ; puis le passage à l'agriculture."],
    ["Hashize imyaka miliyoni 4–2: Australopithecus yagenzaga igororotse; «Lucy» (Etiyopiya, nka miliyoni 3.2) ni skeleton izwi.", "Hashize imyaka miliyoni 2.4–1.5: Homo habilis yakoze ibikoresho by'amabuye; Homo erectus (guhera nka miliyoni 1.9) yakoresheje umuriro ikava muri Afurika.", "Neanderthals babaga i Burayi no mu burengerazuba bwa Aziya kugeza hashize imyaka nka 40,000; abantu benshi hanze ya Afurika bafite 1–2% bya ADN ya Neanderthal.", "Hashize imyaka 40,000–10,000: ibishushanyo mu buvumo, gushyingura, amato; hanyuma kwimukira ku buhinzi."],
    ["Takriban miaka milioni 4–2 iliyopita: Australopithecus walitembea wima; 'Lucy' (Ethiopia, takriban miaka milioni 3.2) ni mifupa maarufu.", "Takriban miaka milioni 2.4–1.5: Homo habilis alitengeneza zana za mawe; Homo erectus (kutoka takriban milioni 1.9) alitumia moto na kuhama Afrika.", "Neanderthals waliishi Ulaya na Asia magharibi hadi takriban miaka 40,000 iliyopita; watu wengi nje ya Afrika wana 1–2% ya DNA ya Neanderthal.", "Takriban miaka 40,000–10,000 iliyopita: sanaa ya mapangoni, mazishi, mashua; kisha kuhamia kilimo."])),
]
